      ],
      "image": "assets/images/218350/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk soy sauce, brown sugar, sherry, mustard, and garlic powder together in a bowl until combined.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/F32bEqgms9LCSNy-ug3WhVUcZyI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/218350_SimpleMarinatedChickenWings_step2_ddmfs_4x3_1221-00a6425cb65d4ba98f26759b09a6447e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/218350/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arrange chicken wings in a 9x13-inch baking dish; pour marinade over chicken and cover with plastic wrap. Marinate in the refrigerator for at least 2 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sKOXfTucwUmYYZclggJmLWpAYF4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/218350_SimpleMarinatedChickenWings_step3_ddmfs_4x3_1224-c4ae1615c6134faf8e69023b44ef3e79.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/218350/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Remove plastic wrap from the baking dish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven, basting occasionally, until chicken wings are no longer pink in the center, about 1 hour. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
